5689600,27.54],[1738368000,20.17],[1740787200,25.22],[1743465600,21.91],[1746057600,22.95],[1748736000,19.77],[1751328000,21.52],[1754006400,20.61],[1756684800,20.63],[1759276800,16.09],[1761955200,22.11],[1764547200,20.3],[1767225600,20.67],[1769904000,22.21],[1772323200,19.19],[1775001600,21.21],[1777593600,18.94],[1780272000,20.31],[1782864000,19.11],[1785542400,19.99],[1788220800,17.98]]}]}],"qna":[{"question":"What is this series?","answer":"It is the monthly total of transactions routed over UPI, the NPCI-run instant payment system, as reported to the RBI by banks and payment providers.^Volume is shown in lakh transactions (1 lakh = 0.1 million) and value in Rs. crore. The USSD line is the small part made through the feature-phone *99# channel."},{"question":"How should I read it?","answer":"Volume growth reflects adoption and frequency of small payments; value growth additionally reflects the average ticket size. Year-on-year growth is the cleanest comparison because of day-count and festival effects: months differ in number of days (February is short) and the festive season lifts October-November.^Value per transaction (value divided by volume) falling over time means UPI is increasingly used for tiny payments."},{"question":"Caveats and revisions?","answer":"RBI figures are provisional and revised in later monthly releases. UPI data here are RBI's compilation and can differ slightly from the figures NPCI publishes on its own site (which also counts some categories differently).^History on the RBI Payment System Indicators pages starts June 2021; earlier months are not on those pages. RBI data are provisional and are revised in later releases; the dashboard keeps the latest revision seen. Counts are transactions processed by the system, not unique users or goods purchased."}],"related":[],"layer":"added","note":"Source: RBI monthly Payment System Indicators (provisional, revised in later releases). Volume is in lakh (1 lakh = 100,000 = 0.1 million) transactions; value in Rs. crore (1 crore = 10 million). Published roughly a month after the reference month; history on the RBI site starts June 2021.","scraped_at":"2026-10-30T07:24:26+00:00"}